{
  "subject": "Basic Mathematics",
  "topic": "Vectors",
  "introduction": "Vectors have both magnitude and direction. In SIMAK, vector problems typically involve expressing a point's position using vector equations (like area ratios), dot products, cross products, and projections. Mastering how vector coefficients relate to area ratios is essential.",
  "key_formulas": [
    {
      "name": "Vector magnitude",
      "formula": "|\\vec{a}| = \\sqrt{a_x^2 + a_y^2}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Dot product",
      "formula": "\\vec{a}\\cdot\\vec{b} = |\\vec{a}||\\vec{b}|\\cos\\theta = a_x b_x + a_y b_y"
    },
    {
      "name": "Cross product (2D)",
      "formula": "|\\vec{a}\\times\\vec{b}| = |a_x b_y - a_y b_x|"
    },
    {
      "name": "Area of parallelogram",
      "formula": "A = |\\vec{a}\\times\\vec{b}|"
    },
    {
      "name": "Area of triangle",
      "formula": "A = \\frac{1}{2}|\\vec{a}\\times\\vec{b}|"
    },
    {
      "name": "Unit vector",
      "formula": "\\hat{a} = \\frac{\\vec{a}}{|\\vec{a}|}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Projection",
      "formula": "\\text{proj}_{\\vec{b}}\\vec{a} = \\frac{\\vec{a}\\cdot\\vec{b}}{|\\vec{b}|^2}\\vec{b}"
    }
  ],
  "tips_and_tricks": [
    "If point P divides AB in ratio m:n, then OP = (n×OA + m×OB)/(m+n).",
    "If OP = αOA + βOB where α+β=1, then P is on line AB.",
    "Area ratio from vector coefficients: if OP = αOA + βOB, the ratios relate to areas of sub-triangles.",
    "Perpendicular vectors: dot product = 0.",
    "Parallel vectors: cross product = 0 (or one is scalar multiple of other).",
    "The angle between two vectors: cosθ = (a·b)/(|a||b|)."
  ],
  "worked_examples": [
    {
      "title": "Example 1: Area ratio using vectors",
      "question": "In triangle OAB, point P inside satisfies OP = (2/5)OA + (1/5)OB. Find the ratio of areas [OAP]:[OBP]:[OAB].",
      "solution": [
        "Step 1: OP = (2/5)OA + (1/5)OB. Note coefficients: α=2/5, β=1/5, and α+β=3/5 ≠ 1.",
        "Step 2: This means P is not simply on AB but inside the triangle.",
        "Step 3: For a point P with OP = αOA + βOB: area ratios are determined by coefficients.",
        "Step 4: [OAP]/[OAB] = β = 1/5. [OBP]/[OAB] = α = 2/5. [ABP]/[OAB] = 1-α-β = 2/5.",
        "Step 5: Check: 2/5+1/5+2/5 = 5/5 = 1 of total area. ✓"
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Example 2: Finding angle using dot product",
      "question": "Find the angle between a=(3,4) and b=(1,2).",
      "solution": [
        "Step 1: a·b = 3(1)+4(2) = 11.",
        "Step 2: |a| = √(9+16) = 5. |b| = √(1+4) = √5.",
        "Step 3: cosθ = 11/(5√5) = 11/(5√5).",
        "Step 4: θ = arccos(11/(5√5)) ≈ arccos(0.983) ≈ 10.3°."
      ]
    }
  ],
